  "title":            "Basic Multimodal Scene Editing V1.5",

  "Header":           "OSD-BME-V1.5",
  "Identifier":       {"ImplementerID": "/* String assigned by IIDRA */", "ImplementationID": "/* String assigned by Implementer */", "AIMName": "/* The name of the AIM, given by the concatenation of the two strings ImplementerID and ImplementationID, in this order, with no space and no character between them. */"},

  "APIProfile":       "Basic",
  "Description":      "Basic Multimodal Scene Editing: Basic Scenes and Basic Objects of at least two media - Audio, Visual, Speech, LiDAR, 3D Model, RADAR, Ultrasound, Offline Map - composed into a Basic Multimodal Scene (a voice over music is a BMS of a BAS and a BSS, or of a BAO and a BSO). It is Multimodal Scene Editing (OSD-MSE) working on the Basic Scenes and Basic Objects: each of its two Scene Ports takes a Basic Scene of any medium, each of its two Object Ports a Basic Object of any medium, and the User Command (with the User PoV, optional) places, moves, changes and removes them in the one open Basic Multimodal Scene; the User Command with its response leaves on the second output.",

  "InternalTypes":   [ ],

